From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:39:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Stop restarting a controller that never
 delivers a frame

The control-only stall recovery bounds failed boots within one recovery
(three attempts), but not repeated successful ones: a controller that
boots fine and then stalls again without a single valid frame is
restarted forever, every few seconds, for as long as it stalls.

Count the recoveries since the last valid frame and give up after five,
leaving the interrupt masked with an error in the log. Any valid frame
resets the count, and so does a resume, which boots the controller from
scratch. An idle controller is unaffected: it raises no interrupts, so
it never enters the stall detector.

This closes the gap the stall recovery left open (repeated successful
recoveries followed by another stall). Measured on the iPhone 8 Plus
(D21), where a wedged controller restart-looped until the cap stopped
it.

Originally from iPhOmarchy patches/0042 ("input: apple_z2: D21 bounded
runtime recovery (Orchard 79f5e69 port)", 170831592b6a, its
APPLE_Z2_D21_MAX_DEAD_RESTARTS) and fix 4 of PR-to-Orchard/README.md
(iPhOmarchy 5921728).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
index b13901d3e..a4201ca80 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@
 #define APPLE_Z2_CONTROL_GAP_MS          250
 #define APPLE_Z2_CONTROL_RESTARTS        3
 #define APPLE_Z2_CONTROL_RETRY_MS        1000
+#define APPLE_Z2_CONTROL_RECOVERIES      5
 #define APPLE_Z2_CMD_SIZE                16
 #define APPLE_Z2_RAW_XFER_MAX_SIZE       64
 #define APPLE_Z2_GEN2_MIN_RESULT_SIZE    64
@@ -243,6 +244,7 @@ struct apple_z2 {
 	bool boot_due;		/* resumed: boot once every device is back */
 	unsigned int rearm_attempts;
 	unsigned int control_reads;
+	unsigned int stall_recoveries;	/* restarts since the last frame */
 	unsigned long control_since;
 	unsigned long control_last;
 	bool recovering;
@@ -1925,6 +1927,8 @@ static bool apple_z2_control_stalled(struct apple_z2 *z2)
 	    z2->protocol_state != APPLE_Z2_STATE_REPORTS_READY)
 		return false;
 
+	if (z2->runtime_frame_valid)
+		z2->stall_recoveries = 0;
 	if (!z2->runtime_control_reply || z2->runtime_frame_valid ||
 	    z2->runtime_queue_empty) {
 		z2->control_reads = 0;
@@ -2220,11 +2224,22 @@ static void apple_z2_queue_control_recovery(struct apple_z2 *z2)
 	if (z2->recovering || z2->stopping)
 		return;
 
-	dev_warn_ratelimited(&z2->spidev->dev,
-			     "control-only touch stall, restarting\n");
 	apple_z2_release_contacts(z2);
 	z2->irq_on = false;
 	disable_irq_nosync(z2->spidev->irq);
+	/*
+	 * Restarts that boot but never deliver a frame would otherwise loop
+	 * for as long as the controller stalls. Any frame resets the count.
+	 */
+	if (z2->stall_recoveries >= APPLE_Z2_CONTROL_RECOVERIES) {
+		dev_err(&z2->spidev->dev,
+			"touch stalled again after %u restarts without a frame, giving up\n",
+			z2->stall_recoveries);
+		return;
+	}
+	z2->stall_recoveries++;
+	dev_warn_ratelimited(&z2->spidev->dev,
+			     "control-only touch stall, restarting\n");
 	z2->recovering = true;
 	z2->rearm_attempts = 0;
 	schedule_delayed_work(&z2->rearm_work, 0);
@@ -4597,6 +4612,7 @@ static int apple_z2_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 	z2->stopping = false;
 	z2->recovering = false;
+	z2->stall_recoveries = 0;
 	z2->boot_due = true;
 	return 0;
 }
